          "A generated column (STORED) is computed from other columns and stays consistent: a full name from first and last, a normalized email, a tsvector. You can index it. VIRTUAL in newer versions takes no space, but is not always indexed the same way. A pg_trgm trigram index (GIN/GiST) speeds ILIKE '%fragment%', similarity, and typos (`%` and `<%`) — what FTS does not cover as autocomplete. Do not put trgm on huge text without a need: the index bloats. For 'almost like' addresses and names, trgm is often better than FTS. Agree COLLATE and the extension in a migration, not by hand on one replica.",
